<section class="panel form-panel"><h2>Email password reset</h2><p class="muted">Email code recovery is enabled by default on the login page. Use an authorized sender mailbox on your hosting domain. Your server’s PHP mail service must be configured; mail acceptance does not guarantee inbox delivery. Back up the database before first enabling this feature.</p><form method="post"><?php hiddenAction('password_reset_settings') ?><label>Password recovery<select name="password_reset_enabled"><option value="1">Enabled (default)</option><option value="0" <?= setting($db,'password_reset_enabled')==='0'?'selected':'' ?>>Disabled</option></select></label><label>Sender email address<input type="email" name="password_reset_sender" maxlength="150" value="<?= e(setting($db,'password_reset_sender')) ?>" placeholder="no-reply@your-domain.example"><small>Leave blank to use the installation notification email, or the first admin email.</small></label><button class="primary">Save password reset settings</button></form></section>
